   "he": "רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר אוֹמֵר: אַף עַל פִּי וְכוּ׳. אָמַר רַב יְהוּדָה אָמַר רַב: הֲלָכָה כְּרַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר בְּגִיטִּין. כִּי אַמְרִיתַהּ קַמֵּיהּ דִּשְׁמוּאֵל, אָמַר: אַף בִּשְׁטָרוֹת.",
   "en": "§ It is stated in the mishna that «Rabbi Elazar says: Even if» there are no signatures of witnesses on the document, but rather he handed it to her in the presence of two witnesses, it is a valid bill of divorce. «Rav Yehuda said» that «Rav said» that «the halakha is in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Elazar with regard to bills of divorce.» But «when I said this» halakha «before Shmuel, he said» that the halakha is in accordance with Rabbi Elazar «with regard to» monetary «documents as well.»"
  }
